  "source_excerpts": {
    "title": "Fill-budgeted elimination of large-prime relation components",
    "mechanism": "Object: a bounded-fill elimination forest on auxiliary relation columns. Operation set Sigma: pivot an auxiliary column, merge its incident equations, and project the certified result to base columns. Trichotomy: coordinate-dependent; this is a solver/representation object, not a lossy quotient under the full group translation action. Discarded information: auxiliary logarithm variables are eliminated; combination coefficients retain a group-verifiable certificate. Collect partial relations with at most two auxiliary points from a separately priced large-prime set. Maintain components with exact modular coefficients and only eliminate pivots whose predicted fill remains under f_max. Compare cheap cycles, deferred dense cores and discarded components by cost per independent projected row. The added mechanism is adaptive algebraic sparsification with a proof of the exact projection, not raw cycle counting.",
    "minimal_test": {
      "design": "Toy generated prime-field curves N about 2^12..2^20, m=3, two fixed auxiliary-set sizes, f_max=8,16,32; 20 independent row streams per cell.",
      "execution_status": "design_only_not_approved",
      "controls": [
        {
          "kind": "baseline",
          "design": "Forbid partial relations and auxiliary pivots to recover full-relation collection; permit every pivot to recover standard elimination on the same input matrix."
        },
        {
          "kind": "matched_null",
          "design": "Random sparse matrices with matched row weights and component sizes; same group-valid relations in random arrival order."
        },
        {
          "kind": "known_false",
          "design": "A cycle with coefficients whose determinant vanishes mod N must not yield an independent base relation."
        },
        {
          "kind": "identity",
          "design": "Use the stated baseline slice with identical inputs, ordering and certificate policy; output identities must match exactly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "generic_group",
          "design": "For any claimed group information gain, repeat the statistic on relabelled Z/NZ with the same incidence and acquisition budget. Algebra-only comparisons explicitly do not claim a generic-group escape."
        }
      ],
      "required_metrics": [
        "projected rank, fill per pivot, discarded acquisition cost, total stopped work",
        "all setup, acquisition, unsuccessful-attempt, transport, certificate and verification costs",
        "peak resident memory and total stored bytes",
        "SAT and UNSAT costs separately, or successful and failed incidence attempts separately",
        "loss L=log2(number of represented preimages) and branching b=max verified successors at each retained synopsis; witness storage separately"
      ],
      "budget": {
        "proposed_only": true,
        "maximum_runs": 0,
        "note": "This handoff approves zero runs. A successor needs a new frozen per-cell budget; planning allowance 3 implementation-days and up to 4 CPU-hours/32 GiB for first complete toy cell, scaled only by Coordinator approval. Exhaustive synthetic calibrators may warrant smaller documented bounds."
      },
      "stopping_rules": [
        "Stop on first soundness/completeness control failure and classify the instrument invalid.",
        "At a frozen resource cap report failed_infrastructure without a mathematical verdict.",
        "If valid completed cells miss the quantitative threshold, reject only this mechanism/parameter claim and retain the measured obstruction."
      ],
      "required_artifacts": [
        "frozen source formula/curve/base and seeds",
        "all candidate descriptions and failed attempts",
        "exact control and solution certificates",
        "stage-cost and memory records",
        "independent checker source binding",
        "unpooled raw metrics"
      ]
    },
    "falsification_conditions": [
      "Any valid completed cell exhibits the known-false failure: A cycle with coefficients whose determinant vanishes mod N must not yield an independent base relation.",
      "The completed controlled ladder fails the proposed effect: Total cost <=0.8 fixed policy and memory <=same cap, with no rank counted before projection",
      "The charged saving disappears after including construction, canonicalization, failed attempts, memory or recovery.",
      "A purported synopsis merges the collision pair without retaining its distinction: Same hypergraph cycle count with different coefficient ranks must be distinguished."
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Public generated mathematical instances only, with frozen field, subgroup, curve, factor-base definition, presentation, solver and sample law.",
      "F2 factor-base decomposition is a component, not the proposed new object; the added object is a bounded-fill elimination forest on auxiliary relation columns. F1 generic search is a comparator; any F7 caching/preprocessing is fully charged.",
      "All identity, soundness and completeness certificates must be independently checked before measuring cost.",
      "Prime-field digit/implicit membership is a high-degree or implicit-description escape class of KN-OPEN-020, not a bounded-degree plane-locus exemption. Binary arms use actual Weil descent and never transfer Boolean identities to F_p."
    ],
    "proof_search_map": {
      "bottleneck": "The exact load-bearing step is producing and using a bounded-fill elimination forest on auxiliary relation columns cheaply enough for: Total cost <=0.8 fixed policy and memory <=same cap, with no rank counted before projection",
      "baseline_embedding": {
        "parameter_slice": "Forbid partial relations and auxiliary pivots to recover full-relation collection; permit every pivot to recover standard elimination on the same input matrix.",
        "reproduction_check": "First prove this equality symbolically; in a successor compare every output/certificate at the smallest exhaustive fixture. No reproduction was executed in this task."
      },
      "observation_collision": {
        "observable": "a bounded-fill elimination forest on auxiliary relation columns",
        "distinct_preimage_search": "Same hypergraph cycle count with different coefficient ranks must be distinguished."
      },
      "constructive_transforms": [
        {
          "transform": "representation_reduction",
          "proposed_object": "a bounded-fill elimination forest on auxiliary relation columns",
          "predicted_gain": "Total cost <=0.8 fixed policy and memory <=same cap, with no rank counted before projection"
        }
      ],
      "quantifier_order": "For every admitted public instance in the frozen parameter family, construct certificates with soundness and completeness; for the preregistered distribution and selected fixed design, H1 predicts Total cost <=0.8 fixed policy and memory <=same cap, with no rank counted before projection. Selection may depend on public parameters and charged calibration, never on hidden scalar labels or evaluation outcomes.",
      "method_ceiling": {
        "strongest_certifiable_claim": "A fill-budget policy can lower total relation collection plus linear algebra cost by >=20% relative to a fixed large-prime/cycle policy at the same memory cap. It need not improve yield or exponent. A successful finite test is scoped evidence only; a uniform asymptotic theorem requires a separate bound on every growth parameter.",
        "nearby_object_control": "A cycle with coefficients whose determinant vanishes mod N must not yield an independent base relation."
      },
      "proof_obligations": [
        {
          "responsibility": "baseline",
          "claim": "Forbid partial relations and auxiliary pivots to recover full-relation collection; permit every pivot to recover standard elimination on the same input matrix."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "correctness",
          "claim": "Prove that pivot an auxiliary column, merge its incident equations, and project the certified result to base columns preserves precisely the asserted solution/row/certificate property, with exact witnesses."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "interface",
          "claim": "Prove recovery after the declared loss: auxiliary logarithm variables are eliminated; combination coefficients retain a group-verifiable certificate; independently verify every final group relation."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "size",
          "claim": "Bound all retained data for a bounded-fill elimination forest on auxiliary relation columns including projected rank, fill per pivot, discarded acquisition cost, total stopped work and certificate storage."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "runtime",
          "claim": "Derive and charge the entire expression: C_aux_set+all partial solves+sum pivot fill operations+LA(projected rows)+target descent+checks; M=components+projected matrix+combination witnesses; data=discarded as well as accepted components."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "success_probability",
          "claim": "A bounded-fill policy retains >=80% of informative projected rank while reducing elimination nonzeros by >=40% on the declared relation stream. Establish or test this separately from runtime and correctness."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "strictness",
          "claim": "Exhibit completed controlled evidence or a theorem for Total cost <=0.8 fixed policy and memory <=same cap, with no rank counted before projection; equal solution count or low output degree alone does not establish it."
        }
      ],
      "not_applicable_reason": null
    },
    "interpretation_limits": [
      "Proposals only: no experiment, proof validation, asymptotic improvement, verified novelty, hypothesis transition or goal completion.",
      "All cost inequalities are targets or conditional algebraic accounting, not measurements. Matched Pollard rho O(N^(1/2)) group operations, small memory; BSGS O(N^(1/2)) time and memory. These generic reference rows do not establish that the proposed method wins.",
      "R3 labels the attacked representation stage, not a new group law. Loss or branching must be certified against Sigma; no full-translation quotient claim.",
      "Degree, reduced-basis size, rank deficit, first fall and actual solving work are distinct. The known shared S_4 defect record must be audited before reusing any old implementation.",
      "Negative evidence would concern the exact tested representation, operations, domain and budget-independent completed cells only."
